      "audio": {
        "id": "subtitle-clock-beat-1"
      },
      "narration": "This saddle’s two central slices follow perpendicular directions in the horizontal plane. On the blue slice, y is zero, so z is x squared. On the gold slice, x is zero, so z is negative y squared. Compare the tangents as both points move from the origin toward positive x and positive y. The blue tangent tilts uphill; the gold tangent tilts downhill, both increasingly steeply. Their slopes start at zero. On the negative halves, slope signs reverse, but the bending does not.",
      "visualDescription": "Content needed: One continuous 3D view of z = x² − y², keeping the same surface visible throughout. Reveal the central sections y = 0 in BLUE and x = 0 in GOLD, with perpendicular traces in the horizontal plane. Compare tangent slopes using paired points (t, 0, t²) and (0, t, −t²), moving from the origin toward positive coordinates. Allow observation during the comparison sentence before confirming the signs. Finally inspect negative-coordinate locations to distinguish slope sign from bending. Keep both sections visible and enable geometry-targeted model orbit.\nNotes: Subtitles only; no title card. Approximately 42 seconds at 145 words per minute with reading allowance; actual alignment determines duration. No explicit silence. Main scene orbit false; dedicated model view orbit true, orbitHitTest geometry. No sliders, toggles, or selects.\n",
